<h1>Mirror</h1>
<hr align="left" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from the</span> <span lang="EN-GB" class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Edit</b></span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>menu &gt; Mirror</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">The Mirror function creates a mirrored image of the selected entities in reference to one of the planes of the current co-ordinate system</span><span lang="EN-GB">. The function works with all available entity types.</span></p>
<p><img src="../images/mirror.png" width="188px" height="147px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span>Mirror Plane</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Select as reference one of the planes from the drop-down menu :</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>OXY</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"> mirrors the selection to the OXY plane of the current CS.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>OXZ</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"> mirrors the selection to the OXZ plane of the current CS.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>OYZ</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"> mirrors the selection to the OYZ plane of the current CS.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
